  "articleBody": "While some door hardware installations are pretty straightforward, there are definitely times when bringing in a professional just makes sense. You might think it's a simple swap, but if your door needs new drilling for different hardware, that's where things can get tricky. Precision is key, and an incorrect cut can be costly to fix.\n\nAnother big signal is if your new hardware needs to align with a nonstandard door prep. Most doors are prepped for common hardware, but if yours is unique, a professional can ensure everything fits perfectly without damaging your door or the new hardware. This is especially true for commercial, heavy, or expensive doors where a mistake would be a significant setback.\n\nSo, if you're looking at your project and feeling a bit overwhelmed by measurements, drilling, or ensuring a perfect alignment, don't hesitate to reach out. HH Remodeling LLC can handle these nuances in the Denver area, making sure your new easy-grip door hardware is installed correctly and efficiently, saving you time and potential headaches.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}